## Claim
Text: "Prominent US Democrat party members including Hillary and Bill Clinton, were running a child sex-trafficking ring in the basement of a Washington, D.C., pizzeria."
Claim date: October 18, 2020

## Initial Q&A
### Which specific Washington, D.C. pizzeria is alleged to have hosted the child sex-trafficking ring involving Hillary Clinton and Bill Clinton?
Answer: The Washington, D.C. pizzeria alleged to have hosted the child sex-trafficking ring is "Comet Ping Pong." According to the search result, the fake conspiracy theory reported the restaurant "as the front for a child-trafficking ring headed by Hillary Clinton and her campaign chief, John D. Podesta."

Source URL: https://www.oxygen.com/very-real/fake-news-accused-hillary-clinton-of-sex-crimes-and-ruined-this-pizzeria

### Does the Washington, D.C. pizzeria Comet Ping Pong, which is central to these allegations, actually have a basement or any underground facilities?
Answer: No, the Washington, D.C. pizzeria Comet Ping Pong does not actually have a basement or any underground facilities. According to the provided source, despite the conspiracy theory's claims, the establishment "doesn’t even have a basement."

Source URL: https://www.thecut.com/2016/12/to-understand-pizzagate-it-helps-to-understand-cults.html

### What official findings or statements have law enforcement agencies released regarding the allegations of a child sex-trafficking ring at Comet Ping Pong?
Answer: According to police statements, the allegations of a child sex-trafficking ring at Comet Ping Pong were characterized as a "fake news story" and a "fake news conspiracy theory." Furthermore, following the arrest of an armed man who attempted to investigate the conspiracy theory at the restaurant, a "police sweep of the area found nothing hazardous."

Source URL: https://www.nbcwashington.com/news/local/man-with-assault-rifle-arrested-at-comet-ping-pong-in-nw-dc/111295/

### Is there any credible physical, digital, or forensic evidence linking Hillary Clinton or Bill Clinton to the operations of Comet Ping Pong or any other Washington, D.C. pizzeria?
Answer: Based on the provided search result, there is no credible evidence linking Hillary Clinton to Comet Ping Pong or any other pizzeria. The article characterizes these allegations as a "debunked conspiracy theory" and "false rumor" that originated from "fake news stories" on online message boards, noting that the gunman who entered the restaurant was attempting to "self-investigate" these entirely false claims.

Source URL: https://www.csmonitor.com/USA/2016/1205/Gunman-at-Comet-Ping-Pong-sought-to-self-investigate-fake-Clinton-report

### Are there any documented police reports, court cases, or official complaints filed by victims or witnesses regarding child sex-trafficking at Comet Ping Pong?
Answer: Based on the provided search result, there is no mention of any documented police reports, court cases, or official complaints filed by victims or witnesses regarding child sex-trafficking at Comet Ping Pong. Instead, the article notes that "no proof was ever presented to support the allegations," and D.C. police dismissed the claims as "fictitious." Furthermore, an armed man who stormed the restaurant to search for underage sex slaves ultimately surrendered to police, "admitting he’d found no evidence that anyone was being harmed in the pizzeria."

Source URL: https://www.pmq.com/the-lessons-of-pizzagate/

### What is the origin of the claim that Hillary Clinton and Bill Clinton were running a child sex-trafficking ring out of a Washington, D.C. pizzeria, and how did it spread online?
Answer: The conspiracy theory, known as "Pizzagate," originated on October 30, 2016, when a "white supremacist Twitter account" and a poster on the conspiracy website Godlike Productions falsely claimed that emails from Clinton aide Huma Abedin and her husband Anthony Weiner contained evidence of an "international child enslavement ring" centered around Hillary Clinton. The rumor spread rapidly as chatter on "4chan, Twitter, Reddit and Facebook" filtered down to right-wing blogs and pro-Trump websites. The connection to the Washington, D.C. pizzeria, Comet Ping Pong, was established in early November 2016 when users began searching leaked WikiLeaks emails from Clinton campaign chief John Podesta, speculating that words like "pizza" and "cheese pizza" were secret code words for child trafficking and alleging that correspondence between the restaurant's owner and Democratic operatives contained clues to the ring.

Source URL: https://www.billboard.com/music/rb-hip-hop/teigen-legend-pizzagate-conspiracy-timeline-8085816/

### Have any prominent US Democratic Party members been arrested, indicted, or convicted in connection with a child sex-trafficking ring operating in Washington, D.C.?
Answer: No. According to the provided search result, claims that prominent politicians like the Clintons have been arrested or are under house arrest for child sex trafficking are "rooted in conspiracy theories that are supported by no evidence." Furthermore, the "Pizzagate" conspiracy theory alleging a child sex ring in a Washington, D.C. pizzeria was a "baseless suggestion," and police found "no evidence that underage children were being harbored in the restaurant" when investigating the site.

